      "text": [
        " قُلْتُ لِأَبِي عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) أَيُّ شَيْ‏ءٍ لِلْمَوَالِي فَقَالَ لَيْسَ لَهُمْ مِنَ الْمِيرَاثِ إِلَّا مَا قَالَ اللَّهُ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ إِلَّا أَنْ تَفْعَلُوا إِلى أَوْلِيائِكُمْ مَعْرُوفاً ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya and others, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad, from Al Hassan Bin Al Jaham, from Hanan who said, ",
          "‘I said to Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup>, ‘Which thing is for the Mawla (Master)?’ So he<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘There is nothing for them from the inheritance except what Allah<sup>azwj</sup> Mighty and Majestic has Said <span class=\"ibTxt\"><a href=\"/#/books/quran:33#h6\"><a href=\"/books/quran:33#h6\">[33:6]</a></a> except that you should do good to your guardians</span>’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "3. Muhammad ibn Yahya and others have narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad from al-Hassan ibn al-Jahm from Hanan who has narrated the following: “I once asked abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, about what is for a Mawla ’ (Master). He (the Imam) said, ‘There is nothing for them (Mawla’ (Masters)) except what Allah, most Majestic, most Glorious, has said, ‘. . . except if you do well-liked favor to your guardians.’ <a href=\"/#/books/quran:33#h6\"><a href=\"/books/quran:33#h6\">[33:6]</a></a>” "
        ]
      }
    },
